{%- comment -%}
  fye-finder-entry — the way in to the ring matchmaker. Intended uses: the
  homepage and the engagement / wedding / eternity ring pages, and anywhere
  else a visitor is likely to stall.

  NOT A BUTTON, and not a popup (Ed, 04/09/2026). It shows the same journey
  tiles the matchmaker itself opens on, each deep-linked with ?j=<key>, so a
  visitor on the engagement rings page lands on the fork rather than on
  question one. Two reasons that beat a modal: the results screen is two
  full-width columns with a product grid and a four-field form, which a dialog
  turns into a scroll inside a scroll; and a page has a URL, so it can be
  shared, measured step by step, and found in search.

  The eyebrow carries the NAME and the heading carries the PROMISE — "Find or
  Design Your Perfect Ring" — because the name's job is to differentiate in
  the menu, not to headline a section. Both are settings; change them here and
  on the matchmaker page together.

  The ?j= keys must match the journey block keys in the matchmaker section
  (eng / plain / dia). A key with no match simply opens on the first question,
  which is a survivable failure — assets/fye-ui.js warns in the console.

  One tile is fine: on the engagement rings page a single "start here" tile
  reads better than three, two of which are the wrong category. The tile row
  CENTRES, so hiding a journey does not leave a hole in the grid — the third
  tile is deliberately out of block_order on the homepage until the eternity
  path is right (Ed, 10/09/2026).

  URL, 10/09/2026: the page moved to /pages/design-your-own-ring. The default
  below has to be the new path, because a redirect does NOT carry the ?j= query
  string with it — the old default sent every tile to question one.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.band | default: 'white'
  assign base = s.page_url | default: '/pages/design-your-own-ring'
  assign cols = section.blocks.size | at_least: 1
-%}

<section class="mme band band--{{ band }}" data-screen-label="Matchmaker entry">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- if s.eyebrow != blank or s.heading != blank or s.intro != blank -%}
      <div class="sect-head">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}<h2 class="heading-flank">{{ s.heading }}</h2>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.intro != blank -%}<p class="lead">{{ s.intro }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ul class="mme__tiles" style="--mme-cols: {{ cols }};">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign b = block.settings
            assign href = base
            if b.journey != blank
              assign href = base | append: '?j=' | append: b.journey
              if b.start != blank
                assign href = href | append: '&start=' | append: b.start
              endif
            endif
          -%}
          <li class="mme__item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <a class="mme__tile" href="{{ href }}">
              {%- if b.icon != blank -%}
                <img class="mme__icon" src="{{ b.icon | file_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="68" height="68" loading="lazy">
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="mme__name">{{ b.label | default: 'Start here' }}</span>
              {%- if b.description != blank -%}
                <span class="mme__desc">{{ b.description }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
              <span class="mme__go link">{{ b.cta | default: s.cta | default: 'Begin' }}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- else -%}
      <p class="lead center">Add a tile for each journey this section should open.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* CLASS PREFIX IS mme, NOT fnd — 10/09/2026, and this is load-bearing.

   Another component in this theme owns .fnd and sets display: grid on it,
   with roughly two columns. Because every section stylesheet block is
   concatenated into one document stylesheet, that rule reached this section
   as well: the band became a two-column grid, .wrap became a start-packed
   grid item in a content-sized first column, and the section rendered 759px
   wide against the left edge with a 1,048px empty column beside it. The
   flanked heading lost its hairlines at the same time, because they are
   flex: 1 1 0 and had no spare width to grow into.

   margin-inline: auto could not save it: an auto margin cannot centre an item
   inside a track only as wide as its own content. Nor could specificity —
   .fye .fnd declared twice means the later rule wins, and section stylesheet
   order is not ours to choose. Renaming removes the collision outright, which
   is the honest fix anyway: two unrelated components should not share a root
   class. --cols is renamed for the same reason, since .fye .agrid reads it
   with a fallback of 4. */
.fye .mme { display: block; width: 100%; }
.fye .mme > .wrap { max-width: var(--maxw); width: 100%; margin-inline: auto; }

.fye .mme__tiles {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: grid;
  /* Tracks are BOUNDED rather than 1fr, and the row is centred. With 1fr the
     tracks always fill the measure, so a section showing two of its three
     journeys left an empty column on the right and the row read as
     left-aligned. Bounded tracks plus justify-content mean any number of tiles
     from one to four sits centred, at a consistent tile width. */
  grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--mme-cols, 3), minmax(0, 380px));
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--grid-gap);
}
.fye .mme__item { margin: 0; display: flex; }
/* Same tile as the matchmaker's own journey cards, so arriving there feels
   like continuing rather than starting again. The CTA sits at the bottom on
   its own row: margin-top auto keeps it level across tiles of unequal copy. */
.fye .mme__tile {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s3);
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 44px;
  padding: var(--s6);
  border: var(--hairline);
  background: var(--white);
  color: var(--ink);
  transition: border-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .band--white .mme__tile { background: transparent; }
.fye .mme__tile:hover { border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--ink); }
.fye .mme__tile:hover .mme__name,
.fye .mme__tile:hover .mme__go { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .mme__icon { width: 68px; height: 68px; }
.fye .mme__name {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  letter-spacing: 0.07em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}
.fye .mme__desc { font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink-soft); }
.fye .mme__go { margin-top: auto; transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease); }

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  /* Below 900 the tiles fill the measure again: two bounded 380px tracks in a
     narrow viewport would leave the row looking stranded rather than centred. */
  .fye .mme__tiles { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .mme__tiles { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .fye .mme__tile { padding: var(--s5); }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Matchmaker entry",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fye-finder-entry",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The eyebrow carries the name, the heading carries the promise. Keep them in step with the matchmaker page itself." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Design Your Own Ring" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Find or Design Your Perfect Ring" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "intro", "label": "Introduction" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "page_url", "label": "Matchmaker page", "info": "Defaults to /pages/design-your-own-ring. Do not point this at /pages/ring-matchmaker: that path still redirects, but the redirect drops the ?j= journey key and every tile then opens on question one." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta", "label": "Tile link text", "default": "Begin" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "band", "label": "Background", "default": "white",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Champagne ivory" },
        { "value": "mist", "label": "Mist blue" },
        { "value": "teal", "label": "Eternal teal" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "tile",
      "name": "Tile",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Name" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "description", "label": "Description" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "journey", "label": "Journey key", "info": "eng, plain or dia — must match a journey block on the matchmaker page. Leave empty to open on the first question." },
        {
          "type": "select", "id": "start", "label": "Skip the fork", "default": "",
          "info": "Only engagement and diamond journeys have a fork.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "", "label": "Ask where to start" },
            { "value": "setting", "label": "Start with the setting" },
            { "value": "stone", "label": "Start with the stone" }
          ]
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cta", "label": "Link text" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon file name", "info": "A file in Content › Files, including the extension." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Matchmaker entry",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Engagement rings", "journey": "eng" } },
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Plain wedding rings", "journey": "plain" } },
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Diamond and eternity rings", "journey": "dia" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
